#
# sources - Windows 2000 DDK (x86) and WDK 7.1 (amd64) build description
# for xhcicm.sys, the Thunderbolt and USB4 connection manager (design
# records 21 and 22; roadmap-usb4.md task 39-A.1), a second driver beside
# xhci98.sys with its own INFs (xhcicm.inf for the NHI, xhcicmf.inf for
# the NT tunnel-bridge filter, and their -amd64 twins).
#
# Build with scripts\build-driver.cmd, which builds this directory after
# src\uas for every flavour and runs the import gate on the result against
# scripts\import-gate\xhcicm-imports.allow (x86) or
# xhcicm-imports-amd64.allow (amd64). Output: src\cm\objfre\<arch>\
# xhcicm.sys (release) and src\cm\objchk_qemu (qemu).
#
# THE PURE CORE: cm_vals.c (test\test_cm.c); the host interface ring 0,
# the ICM client and the hardware profiles, tbt_ring.c, tbt_icm.c and
# tbt_hw.c (test_tbt_ring, test_tbt_icm, test_tbt_hw, test_tbt_select);
# the USB4 software connection manager, tbt_u4cm.c (test_u4cm; Phase 40,
# design record 22); the inter-domain discovery and USB4NET service it
# drives, tbt_xdp.c (test_tbt_xdp, test_u4xd; task 45.59, design record
# 35); the tunnel ports, tbt_topo.c (test_tbt_topo), the chained
# tunnels' bindings, tbt_chain.c (test_tbt_topo; task 48.30, design record
# 34 section 3.12), and the
# 9x bus numbering of the bridges below them, tbt_brnum.c (test_tbt_brnum;
# record 21 section 6.1.1); the 9x start of a function with no interrupt,
# cm_noirq.c (test_cm_noirq; design record 28); the
# re-enumeration's own pure half, cm_ports.c (test_cm_ports), the
# ACPI-named tunnel-port source's _DSD reader, cm_dsd.c (test_cm_dsd;
# task 46.23, design record 22 section 7.6.1), the
# interrupt of a function hot-added on 2000, cm_irq.c (test_cm_irq; task
# 44.53, record 21 section 6.2.1), the requirement lists of a hot-added
# bridge on 2000 and XP, cm_breq.c (test_cm_breq; task 45.12, design
# record 33), the isolation statement's decision, cm_iso.c (test_cm_iso;
# task 45.35, design record 22 section 10.5), the ring interrupt's pure
# half, cm_rirq.c (test_cm_rirq; task 45.22, design record 21 section
# 4.5; its driver half cm_rirqos.c), the marks
# answer's table, cm_marks.c (test_cm_marks; task 42-A.5), the 9x
# tunnel id's pure half, cm_tagid.c (test_cm_tagid; task 44.3), and the
# query device's answers, cm_query.c, cm_qpci.c, cm_qacpi.c and cm_qnet.c
# (test_cm_query, test_trpci, test_tracpi, test_cm_qnet); the
# shared log ring ..\xhci_log.c (test\test_log.c), compiled in by path; and
# the registry values' precedence, ..\xhci_regsrc.c (test\test_regsrc.c;
# task 42-A.17), compiled in the same way; and the x86 helper's channel,
# ..\xhci_hlpr.c (test\test_msi.c), whose minor 1 cm_oscnt.c asks on
# x86 (task 46.12, design record 32 section 12.8.15.15).
# All DDK-free.
# cm_pool.c is the one file that allocates pool; cm_reg.c and cm_statos.c
# the two that open a registry key through the kernel's imports
# (cm_nvlinkos.c's 9x keys go through the VMM's registry services);
# cm_log.c the one DbgPrint site (every flavour,
# under XhciCmLogDebugView, since the owner's reversal of decision D12 on
# 2026-10-16). The allowlists hold each to its file with SITES=. cm_cfgmg.c is
# the one file that calls CONFIGMG (Windows 98 SE and ME, x86 only).
# cm_call.c is the pure handoff word of the 9x per-member call workers
# (test_cm_call; task 42-A.12), cm_callwk.c their threads.
# cm_eject.c is the pure 9x eject transaction and statement decision
# (test_cm_eject; task 43.18), cm_ejectos.c their driver half.
# cm_pwrr.c is the pure route of a system SET_POWER's device half
# (test_cm_pwrr; task 43.65), cm_power.c its driver half.
# cm_oscp.c is the pure half of the NT handover (test_cm_oscp; task 46.12,
# design record 32 section 12.8.15), cm_oscnt.c its driver half and the
# mailbox members' filters.
#
# ADDING A FILE. A new .c is one more line in SOURCES below (a file of
# src\ by path, as ..\xhci_log.c is); scripts\source-stamp.ps1 reads this
# list, so the stamp follows. Headers (tbt_regs.h, cm_cfgmg.h) need no
# line. A pure file also gets a host suite line in test\run-host-tests.cmd,
# as test_cm has.
#

TARGETNAME=xhcicm
TARGETTYPE=DRIVER
TARGETPATH=obj

INCLUDES=$(BASEDIR)\inc;$(BASEDIR)\inc\ddk

SOURCES=cm_vals.c      \
