!IF "$(XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES)" != ""
!ERROR XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES is set, and xhcicm.sys has no diagnostic builds. Clear it before building.
!ENDIF

#
# The flavours, derived from BUILD_ALT_DIR exactly as src\sources
# derives them for xhci98.sys (design record 08), so the same flavour
# marker check and packaging refusals apply to this binary: release and
# qemu (debug was retired with task 45.45, design record 08 section 14). The
# qemu flavour is a checked build and carries cm_log.c's port-0xE9 mirror of
# the log emission (decision D12), whose WRITE_PORT_UCHAR import is a qemu
# row, and the DebugView sink forced on (cm_log.c, #if DBG).
#
# NTNOFPO: the release flavour keeps frame pointers on the MSVC 6.0 x86
# build (/Oy- and FPO=0; the Windows 2000 DDK's i386mk.inc reads it after
# this file), as the retired debug flavour did (task 45.45, design record 08
# section 14). WDK 7.1 does not read it: its amd64 build has no FPO switch.
!IF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "chk_qemu"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_QEMU
!ELSEIF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "fre"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_RELEASE
NTNOFPO=1
!ELSE
!ERROR BUILD_ALT_DIR is "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" and this tree knows exactly two flavours - fre (release) and chk_qemu (qemu). The debug flavour (chk) was retired with roadmap-usb4 task 45.45 (design record 08 section 14). Build through scripts\build-driver.cmd.
!ENDIF

#
# x86 only. The amd64 images (WDK 7.1) keep .rdata a section of its own,
# so the import address table is not in the executable .text: with it
# there, Driver Verifier's code integrity checks on 10 x64 stop the
# driver as it loads (bug check 0xC4, 0x2005; roadmap-usb4 task 45.63).
#
!IF "$(_BUILDARCH)" != "AMD64"
LINKER_FLAGS=-merge:.rdata=.text
!ENDIF
